separates them both ways. At 0.35 deg only a wind measurement at about 20,000 ft helps, and only one way (it can rule out the balloon, never the slow flier, which may fly at zero air speed). - Glare or physical object. Since the rotation criterion is scored on held-out data (CP-04 fix), it no longer separates them, and the recovery test confirms it (glare-made data are often won by the balloon). A radar range or closure rate separates the glare models from the balloon one way only (the glare models' bands are wide and reach their prior bounds). - Pairs no measurement separates. The distant jet and the glare-on-a-target model are the same physics here. The free path (H-WIT) can sit at any range and speed; its discriminator bands in discriminators.md are degenerate (0 nmi) and are not used here. - Field of view. It does not change the physics-only leader with the exclusions (the balloon at both), but changes its lead over the slow flier from 3.7 to 11.3 log units and moves the balloon's end range in from 15 to 30 nmi to 9 to 14 nmi. - The exclusions. Without the data-quality exclusions the free path leads at both fields of view and the balloon is fifth (results above), so any measurement that settles the size and brightness question (an unsaturated recording) also bears on the ranking."}}